# ---- Results
tb = S5["threshold_bootstrap"]; gb = G5["threshold_bootstrap"]
setl(167, body[166] + f"\n\nThe Wilson interval treats the thresholds as known. They are estimates. When the IHC ER-positive reference was resampled (amendment A5), the 95% interval was {tb['ESR1'][0]:.2f}–{tb['ESR1'][1]:.2f} for the ESR1 threshold and {tb['activity'][0]:.3f}–{tb['activity'][1]:.3f} for the activity threshold, and the HEA count among the 241 tumours was {int(tb['HEA_count_fixed_negatives'][0])}–{int(tb['HEA_count_fixed_negatives'][1])}. With the IHC ER-negative tumours resampled as well, the interval for prevalence was {f1(tb['prevalence_combined_interval'][0])}–{f1(tb['prevalence_combined_interval'][1])}%.")
pr = R1["pairs_in_HEA_range"]; c7, t7 = R7["constant"], R7["tertile"]
setl(200, "### 3.2. Repeatability of the Measurements and Stability of the Calls")
setl(202, f"Three kinds of evidence need to be kept apart.\n\n**Observed repeatability of the measurements.** Both axes were almost perfectly repeatable on re-sequencing across their full range (Table 3; Figure S1). The ICC was 0.991 for ESR1 and 0.997 for the activity score across all 136 replicate pairs, and 0.996 and 0.999 across the 36 cross-platform pairs.\n\n**Observed agreement of calls in replicate pairs.** High/low calls on each axis agreed in 98.5% and 97.8% of pairs (Table 3). The joint \"both high\" call agreed in {R1['pairs'] - R1['discordant']} of {R1['pairs']} pairs (κ {R1['kappa']:.2f}, 95% CI {R1['kappa_ci'][0]:.2f}–{R1['kappa_ci'][1]:.2f}; amendment A5). In all, {pr['n']} pairs lay inside the range of the 20 HEA tumours on both axes, and all {pr['agree_n']} were both-high in both libraries. However, {pr['ihc_er_status_of_originals'].get('1', 0)} of them were IHC ER-positive tumours and the other had missing ER status. Only {R1['neg_pairs_n']} replicate pairs came from IHC ER-negative tumours (10 concordant ER-negative, 3 activity without ESR1). All 13 kept their group, but none was an HEA tumour. No HEA call was therefore re-measured directly.")
setl(204, f"**Simulated stability of the 20 HEA calls.** The replicate-derived technical SD was 0.27 log2 units for ESR1 and 0.0022 for the activity score. On simulated re-measurement, 0.82 of the 20 HEA calls were expected to change, and 18 of 20 had a reclassification probability below 10%. The two unstable calls lay at the ESR1 threshold and were both PAM50 Normal-like. The simulation estimates the probability that a call changes when the same RNA is measured again, given the observed values and additive Gaussian technical error. It does not include sampling or biological variation within a tumour. When the replicate pairs and the IHC ER-positive reference were resampled (amendment A5), so that the SDs, their correlation and the thresholds were re-estimated, the number of HEA tumours with a reclassification probability below 10% was {int(c7['robust_lt10'][0])}–{int(c7['robust_lt10'][1])} (95% interval; lowest value {c7['robust_lt10_min_max'][0]} in 500 resamples), and the expected number of changed calls was {c7['expected_flips_20'][0]:.2f}–{c7['expected_flips_20'][1]:.2f}. The expression-dependent noise model gave {int(t7['robust_lt10'][0])}–{int(t7['robust_lt10'][1])} and {t7['expected_flips_20'][0]:.2f}–{t7['expected_flips_20'][1]:.2f}.")
sc_, gc_ = S5["counts"], G5["counts"]
