setl(257, "As planned, outcomes were reported only as counts. In the HEA group, 19 of 20 patients received chemotherapy, 1 received endocrine therapy and none died during a median follow-up of 3.9 years. In comparison, 23 of 160 concordant ER-negative patients and 11 of 58 with activity without ESR1 died. These numbers are small, follow-up is short and no comparison was made. They do not support any inference about prognosis or endocrine benefit in the HEA group, in either direction.")
setl(259, "### 3.7. Post Hoc Checks (Amendments A2 and A3)")
